---
import DocLayout from '../layouts/DocLayout.astro';
import { email, site } from '../config';
---

<DocLayout
  pointsTitle="The short version"
  points={[
    '**The app collects nothing.** It makes no network connections.',
    '**This website sets no cookies.** It counts visits with Cloudflare Web Analytics, which can’t identify you.',
    '**The only personal data we get** is what you send us, and what Paddle passes on when you buy.',
  ]}
  title="Privacy Policy"
  h1="Stillroom Vault privacy policy"
  eyebrow="Legal"
  description="Stillroom Vault collects nothing: the app makes no network connections, and this website sets no cookies and counts visits without identifying anyone. What Paddle collects when you buy."
  lead="What the app collects (nothing), what this website counts, what Paddle collects when you buy, and your rights."
  updated="29 October 2026"
  legal
>
    <h2 id="who">Who is responsible</h2>
    <p>
      {site.seller}, an individual based in {site.sellerCountry}, is responsible for this website and for the personal
      data described here: its controller, under Kosovo’s Law on the Protection of Personal Data and, where they apply,
      the EU and UK GDPR. Contact: <a href={`mailto:${email.legal}`}>{email.legal}</a>.
    </p>

    <h2 id="app">The app</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Stillroom makes no network connections.</strong> It has no server, no account, no sync, no analytics and
        no crash reporting. Every build is checked and refused if networking code appears in it.
      </li>
      <li>Your vault, its keys and everything in it stay on your Mac. We can’t see or reach any of it.</li>
      <li>
        The activity log, if you turn it on (it’s off by default), stays on your Mac for 7 days and never records typing,
        file names, sizes, passwords or contents. It only leaves your Mac if you choose to send it to us.
      </li>
      <li>
        The intruder log’s photos, if you allow them, are sealed inside your vault, on your Mac.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="website">This website</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        No cookies, no advertising, and nothing that follows you to other sites. The checkout page also loads Paddle’s
        checkout script, which may set cookies of its own when you buy.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>We count visits</strong> with Cloudflare Web Analytics. We need it to know how the site runs, which pages
        people read, and what works and what doesn’t. It records the page you’re on, the site that sent you there, your
        country, your browser and device type, and how fast the page loaded. It sets no cookies, stores nothing in your
        browser and doesn’t fingerprint you, so you can’t be identified from it, by us or anyone else. If your browser or
        an ad blocker stops it, the site works just the same.
      </li>
      <li>
        It’s hosted on Cloudflare Pages. To deliver pages and protect the site from attacks, Cloudflare processes each
        request, including your IP address, under Cloudflare’s own privacy policy. We see totals from that too, such as
        page views and downloads, never who made them.
      </li>
      <li>
        The “Seal it yourself” demo runs in your browser. What you type there is never sent anywhere; the demo doesn’t
        make any request at all.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="buying">When you buy</h2>
    <p>
      Our order process is conducted by our online reseller Paddle.com. Paddle.com is the Merchant of Record for all our
      orders. Paddle provides all customer service inquiries and handles returns.
    </p>
    <p>
      At checkout, Paddle collects what it needs to take payment, charge the right tax and prevent fraud: typically your
      name, email address, country and postcode, payment details, IP address, and a VAT number if you give one. Paddle is
      responsible for that data under <a href="https://www.paddle.com/legal/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">its privacy policy</a>. We never see
      your card details.
    </p>
    <p>Paddle passes us your name, email address, country and what you bought. We use them to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        make and email your licence key, which carries your name, email address, edition, how many people it covers, and
        the order number and date. The server that makes it keeps none of this: it emails the key and forgets it;
      </li>
      <li>answer you about your order, or send your key again if you lose it;</li>
      <li>tell you when a new version is out, since the app never checks for updates itself. You can ask us to stop.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Your name and email address are needed to make and send your licence key; without them we can’t sell you one.
    </p>
    <p>
      We keep order records for as long as tax and accounting law requires, up to 10 years. We delete email
      conversations 2 years after the last message, unless one is still needed for an open order or claim.
    </p>

    <h2 id="email">When you email us</h2>
    <p>
      We get your address and your message, and keep them as long as we need to help you. Please never send us your
      password, recovery key or kit pieces. We’ll never ask for them.
    </p>

    <h2 id="who-else">Who else handles it</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Paddle</strong>: checkout, payment, tax, invoices and refunds, as described above.</li>
      <li><strong>Cloudflare</strong>: hosts this website, counts its visits, and forwards email sent to our addresses to our mailbox.</li>
      <li><strong>Google</strong>: Gmail holds our mailbox, where email to our addresses is forwarded.</li>
      <li><strong>Resend</strong>: sends your licence key, and our emails about new versions.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Some of these process data outside your country, including in the United States. For that we rely on the
      safeguards each offers, such as the European Commission’s standard contractual clauses or the EU–US Data Privacy
      Framework. We never sell personal data or share it for advertising.
    </p>

    <h2 id="bases">Why we may use it</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Sending your licence key and helping with your order: to carry out our agreement with you.</li>
      <li>Telling buyers about new versions: our legitimate interest in keeping you able to update, since the app can’t check. Every such email says how to stop them.</li>
      <li>Keeping order records: what tax law requires.</li>
      <li>Answering your email: our legitimate interest in replying to you.</li>
      <li>Counting visits to this website: our legitimate interest in knowing how the site runs and what works.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="rights">Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      You can ask us what we hold about you, and ask us to correct, export or delete it, to limit how we use it, or object
      to how we use it, at <a href={`mailto:${email.legal}`}>{email.legal}</a>. It’s free, and we answer within one
      month. We may ask you to write from the address in question, so we know it’s you.
    </p>
    <p>
      You can also complain to a data protection authority: in Kosovo, the Information and Privacy Agency; in the EU or
      UK, the authority where you live or work. We’d like the chance to help first.
    </p>

    <h2 id="other">Children, decisions and breaches</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Stillroom isn’t aimed at children under 16, and we don’t knowingly collect their data.</li>
      <li>We make no automated decisions about you and build no profiles.</li>
      <li>
        If a breach ever puts your personal data at risk, we’ll tell you and the authorities, as and when the law
        requires.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="changes">Changes</h2>
    <p>
      If this policy changes, the new version will be posted here with its date. If a change matters for buyers, we’ll
      also email them.
    </p>
</DocLayout>
